From e275e2ccbce97965a8a2bf9cf299b6f161fa9620 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: djvalic <djvalic@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 12:00:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] ad5x: IFS load, unload, eject and tune home an idle printer
 first
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

After a Klipper restart (the setup wizard's last step restarts it)
nothing is homed. Unload on the IFS or Filament screen sent
`IFS_UNLOAD SLOT=n`, which Kiln's module refuses on an unhomed printer:
the user saw at most a short "IFS: home the printer first (G28)" toast
and nothing moved. Eject of the loaded lane and the IFS tuning (it
unloads the loaded slot first) went the same way. A load homed first
(ensure_homed_then), but showed "Heating nozzle" while it did.

The module's IFS_LOAD, IFS_UNLOAD, IFS_EJECT and IFS_TUNE now carry
HOME=1. Kiln's module then homes an idle printer that is not homed
itself, inside the operation (printer.ifs phase homing_printer), and
refuses during a print or a pause with a message that says so. Typed in
the console without HOME=1 the commands only ask for a home, as before.
The module's load no longer sends a G28 of its own (skip_homing): one
homing path, decided by Klipper with the live print state.

The screen shows the homing: phase homing_printer is the first step
(Heat), "· Homing first..." in the line of an operation the module
started, and "Homing first..." in place of the heating line for a load
or unload started from the screen (the phase tracker keeps its steps).
A module phase change counts as progress, so the Heat step doesn't turn
to "Working..." while the printer homes with a nozzle already hot. The
text is the existing key "Homing first..." (en, ru and the other
languages already have it).

zMod's own macros (INSERT_PRUTOK_IFS, _IFS_REMOVE_CURRENT_PRUTOK,
A_CHANGE_FILAMENT) and the module's T<n> are unchanged.

Upstream: not applicable (AD5X OS specific)
